{\rtf1\ansi\uc1{\*\generator WTS5;}\adeflang1025\adeff0\deff0\stshfdbch0\stshfloch0\stshfhich0\deflang1033\deflangfe1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1\fcharset0 Latha;}{\f2\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f3\fcharset0 MEPS Bookman WTS;}{\f4\fbidi\fcharset177 Arial;}}{\colortbl ;\red128\green0\blue128;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green128\blue0;\red33\green88\blue104;\red0\green176\blue80;\red153\green51\blue102;\red102\green102\blue153;\red51\green51\blue204;\red128\green0\blue0;}{\stylesheet {\s2\ltrpar\qc \rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f0\fs36\cf1\b \sbasedon0\snext21 Title;}{\s12\ltrpar\qc \rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\fs24\cf10\b \sbasedon0\snext25 Heading 1;}}\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033\ltrdoc\fcs1\af0\afs24\acf0\fcs0\f0\fs24\cf0{\info\uc1{\upr{\*\ud{\author \u67?\u111?\u112?\u121?\u114?\u105?\u103?\u104?\u116?\u32?\u169?\u32?\u50?\u48?\u50?\u49?\u32?\u87?\u97?\u116?\u99?\u104?\u32?\u84?\u111?\u119?\u101?\u114?\u32?\u66?\u105?\u98?\u108?\u101?\u32?\u97?\u110?\u100?\u32?\u84?\u114?\u97?\u99?\u116?\u32?\u83?\u111?\u99?\u105?\u101?\u116?\u121?\u32?\u111?\u102?\u32?\u80?\u101?\u110?\u110?\u115?\u121?\u108?\u118?\u97?\u110?\u105?\u97?}}}{\upr{\*\ud{\title \u76?\u101?\u115?\u115?\u111?\u110?\u160?\u51?\u57?\u8212?\u71?\u111?\u100?\u8217?\u115?\u32?\u86?\u105?\u101?\u119?\u32?\u111?\u102?\u32?\u66?\u108?\u111?\u111?\u100?}}}}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\s2\qc {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f0\fs36\cf1\b Lesson\u160?39\u8212?God\u8217?s View of Blood\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 Blood is vital. Without it, none of us could live. As the Creator, God has the right to say how blood may be used. What has he said about blood? Can it be eaten or transfused? And how can you make good decisions on this matter?\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2 [Image:]\u160?A microscopic view of the bloodstream.\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ab\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b 1. What is Jehovah\u8217?s view of blood?\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 Jehovah told his worshippers in Bible times: }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ab\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b \u8220?The life of every sort of flesh is its blood.\u8221? }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 (}{\field{\*\fldinst {HYPERLINK "https://www.jw.org/finder?pub=nwtsty&bible=03017014&wtlocale=E&srcid=share" }}{\fldrslt{\cs4\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3\ul Leviticus 17:14}}}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 ) To Jehovah, blood represents life. Since life is a sacred, or holy, gift from God, blood is also sacred.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ab\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b 2. What use of blood does God forbid?\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 Jehovah commanded his pre-Christian worshippers not to eat blood. (Read Genesis 9:4 and Leviticus 17:10.) He confirmed this command when the governing body instructed Christians to }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ab\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b \u8220?keep abstaining .\u160?.\u160?. from blood.\u8221?}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8212?Read }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2 Acts 15:28, 2}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 9.\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af2\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2 [\u8220?Read\u8221? scriptures] Genesis 9:4: Only flesh with its life\u8212?its blood\u8212?you must not eat.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af2\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2 Leviticus 17:10: \u8220?\u8216?If any man of the house of Israel or any foreigner who is residing in your midst eats any sort of blood, I will certainly set my face against the one who is eating the blood, and I will cut him off from among his people.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af2\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2 Acts 15:28, 29: For the holy spirit and we ourselves have favored adding no further burden to you except these necessary things: to keep abstaining from things sacrificed to idols, from blood, from what is strangled, and from sexual immorality. If you carefully keep yourselves from these things, you will prosper. Good health to you!\u8221? [End of \u8220?Read\u8221? scriptures]\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 What does it mean to abstain from blood? If a doctor told you to abstain from alcohol, you would not drink it. But would you eat foods that contained it or have alcohol injected into your veins? Obviously not. Likewise, God\u8217?s command to abstain from blood means that we should not drink blood or eat meat that has not been bled. Nor should we eat any food to which blood has been added.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 What about the medical use of blood? Some procedures clearly violate God\u8217?s law. These include the transfusion of whole blood or any of its main components\u8212?red cells, white cells, platelets, and plasma. Other medical procedures may not be a clear-cut violation of God\u8217?s law. For example, some procedures involve the use of fractions of one of the main components of blood. Other procedures involve the use of a person\u8217?s own blood. When weighing these options, each of us must make a personal decision.\u160?*\u8212?}{\field{\*\fldinst {HYPERLINK "https://www.jw.org/finder?pub=nwtsty&bible=48006005&wtlocale=E&srcid=share" }}{\fldrslt{\cs4\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3\ul Galatians 6:5}}}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 .\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f0\cf2 [Footnote] }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f0\cf4 * See }{\field{\*\fldinst {HYPERLINK "https://www.jw.org/finder?wtlocale=E&docid=1102021235&srcid=share" }}{\fldrslt{\cs4\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f0\cf3\ul Lesson\u160?35}}}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f0\cf4 , \u8220?How to Make Good Decisions.\u8221?}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f0\cf2  [End of footnote]\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 \par\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\qc\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3 Dig Deeper\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 Examine how to make medical decisions regarding the use of blood.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b 3. Make medical decisions that please Jehovah\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 How can you make medical decisions that harmonize with God\u8217?s view? Play the video}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\i  }{\field{\*\fldinst {HYPERLINK "https://www.jw.org/finder?srcid=jwlshare&wtlocale=E&lank=pub-lffv_391_VIDEO" }}{\fldrslt{\cs4\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3\i\ul How to Make Health-Care Decisions Regarding Blood}}}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2  (5:47), and then discuss the importance of taking the steps that follow.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? Pray for wisdom.\u8212?}{\field{\*\fldinst {HYPERLINK "https://www.jw.org/finder?pub=nwtsty&bible=59001005&wtlocale=E&srcid=share" }}{\fldrslt{\cs4\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3\ul James 1:5}}}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 .\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? Research Bible principles and how they apply.\u8212?}{\field{\*\fldinst {HYPERLINK "https://www.jw.org/finder?pub=nwtsty&bible=20013016&wtlocale=E&srcid=share" }}{\fldrslt{\cs4\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3\ul Proverbs 13:16}}}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 .\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? Find out what options are available where you live.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? Identify which options are clearly unacceptable to you.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? Make sure your decision will leave you with a clean conscience.\u8212?}{\field{\*\fldinst {HYPERLINK "https://www.jw.org/finder?pub=nwtsty&bible=44024016&wtlocale=E&srcid=share" }}{\fldrslt{\cs4\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3\ul Acts 24:16}}}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 .\u160?*\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f0\cf2 [Footnote] }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f0\cf4 * See point\u160?5, \u8220?When Blood Fractions Are Involved,\u8221? and }{\field{\*\fldinst {HYPERLINK "https://www.jw.org/finder?wtlocale=E&docid=1102021350&srcid=share" }}{\fldrslt{\cs4\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f0\cf3\ul Endnote\u160?3}}}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f0\cf4 , \u8220?Medical Procedures Involving Blood.\u8221?}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f0\cf2  [End of footnote]\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? Recognize that no one\u8212?not even your spouse, an elder, or your Bible teacher\u8212?should tell you what decision to make in matters of conscience.\u8212?}{\field{\*\fldinst {HYPERLINK "https://www.jw.org/finder?pub=nwtsty&bible=45014012&wtlocale=E&srcid=share" }}{\fldrslt{\cs4\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3\ul Romans 14:12}}}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 .\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? Put your decision in writing.\par}\par\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2 [Image:]\u160?Collage: A man making a medical decision. 1.\u160?He prays. 2.\u160?He does research using the Bible, Bible-based publications, and an electronic tablet. 3.\u160?He talks with his doctor.\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b 4. Jehovah\u8217?s Witnesses seek quality medical care\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 It is possible to adhere to God\u8217?s law about blood and receive quality nonblood medical care. Play the video }{\field{\*\fldinst {HYPERLINK "https://www.jw.org/finder?srcid=jwlshare&wtlocale=E&lank=docid-702018115_1_VIDEO" }}{\fldrslt{\cs4\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3\i\ul Interview of Professor Massimo P.\u160?Franchi,\u160?M.D.}}}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2  (1:36).\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b Read Titus 3:2,}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2  and then discuss this question:\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? Why should we show a cooperative and mild spirit when dealing with medical professionals?\par}\par\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af2\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2 [\u8220?Read\u8221? scripture] Titus 3:2: to speak injuriously of no one, not to be quarrelsome, but to be reasonable, displaying all mildness toward all men. [End of \u8220?Read\u8221? scripture]\par}\par\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b 5. When blood fractions are involved\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 Blood has four main components\u8212?red cells, white cells, platelets, and plasma. These components contain many smaller parts, called blood fractions.\u160?* Some fractions are used in medicines that help to fight diseases or help to stop bleeding.\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f0\cf2 [Footnote] }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f0\cf4 * Some doctors view the four main components of blood as fractions. Therefore, you may need to explain your personal decision not to accept transfusions of whole blood or of red cells, white cells, platelets, or plasma.}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f0\cf2  [End of footnote]\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 When it comes to blood fractions, each Christian must make his own decision based on his Bible-trained conscience. Some may decide to refuse a medical treatment or procedure that involves blood fractions. Others may feel that their conscience allows them to accept fractions.\par}\par\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2 [Image:]\u160?A test tube containing blood separated into its four main components, which are labeled A, B, C, and\u160?D.\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi-720\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf5 Unacceptable\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi-288\li576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf6 A. Blood plasma\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf6 B. White cells\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf6 C. Platelets\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf6 D. Red cells\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi-720\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf5 Christian to decide\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi-288\li576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf6 A. }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf6\b Fractions}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf6  from plasma\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf6 B. }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf6\b Fractions}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf6  from white cells\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf6 C. }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf6\b Fractions}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf6  from platelets\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf6 D. }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf6\b Fractions}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf6  from red cells\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 \par{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 When making your decisions, consider this question:\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? How would I explain to a doctor why I reject or accept the use of certain blood fractions?\par}\par\pa